import{_ as e,o as i,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const h=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 417 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Institutional-Alternative Gains: Injecting Anchor Symbiosis into Manghuang's World","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 417 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Institutional-Alternative Gains: Injecting Anchor Symbiosis into Manghuang's World","no":417,"module":2,"tags":["Manghuang Ji","Institutional-Alternative Gains","Anchor Symbiosis","Quantified","Civilization Reform"],"related":["22-Resource Allocation Joint-Contracting Mechanism","23-20% Activation Strategy Plan","49-Governance Framework and Checks-and-Balances"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0417_模块2-莽荒纪-制度替代收益-锚点共生注入莽荒世界.md","filePath":"en/0417_模块2-莽荒纪-制度替代收益-锚点共生注入莽荒世界.md"}`),a={name:"en/0417_模块2-莽荒纪-制度替代收益-锚点共生注入莽荒世界.md"};function s(r,t,l,c,d,u){return i(),n("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-417-manghuang-system-decomposition-·-institutional-alternative-gains-injecting-anchor-symbiosis-into-manghuang-s-world" tabindex="-1">Entry 417 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Institutional-Alternative Gains: Injecting Anchor Symbiosis into Manghuang&#39;s World <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-417-manghuang-system-decomposition-·-institutional-alternative-gains-injecting-anchor-symbiosis-into-manghuang-s-world" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 417 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Institutional-Alternative Gains: Injecting Anchor Symbiosis into Manghuang&#39;s World&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Manghuang Ji Full Decomposition (Entry 22) | Benchmark base: Documents 22, 23, 49</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-swap-manghuang-s-world-s-institutions-and-see-how-much-civilization-can-rise" tabindex="-1">Introduction: swap Manghuang&#39;s world&#39;s institutions and see how much civilization can rise <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-swap-manghuang-s-world-s-institutions-and-see-how-much-civilization-can-rise" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: swap Manghuang&#39;s world&#39;s institutions and see how much civilization can rise&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The six top-level axioms take the collective ascension axiom as landing point. The previous entry simulated &quot;Ji Ning absent and it collapses&quot;; this entry reverses — <strong>inject Anchor-Symbiosis institutions into Manghuang&#39;s world, quantify how much civilization can rise.</strong> Not replacing Ji Ning, but replacing the set of institutions that &quot;forces Ji Ning to carry it alone.&quot; The law-first axiom requires: injected institutions must legislate first, be recomputable. Protagonist uniqueness dependency: before injection = high-leaning-medium, after = extremely low. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s judging base has been upgraded to the six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The first gain of institutional substitution is the leap in energy utilization efficiency: under Manghuang&#39;s original system, Ji Ning alone locked about 40% of top-tier energy; after injecting joint contracting + 20% activation strategy, this 40% energy is dispersed across a batch of middle tier; civilization overall energy does not drop but rises. <strong>Energy monopolized by one person, distributed to a generation to use, civilization&#39;s total is actually larger.</strong></p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>How institutional substitution eradicates regression:</p><ol><li><strong>Lineage does not go with the person</strong>: Alaya recording makes Great Experts&#39; passing no longer break the lineage</li><li><strong>Great calamities do not zero out</strong>: world backup makes civilization stock recoverable</li><li><strong>Ascend not abandon</strong>: post-duty makes strong ones continuously feed back</li><li><strong>Gain indicator</strong>: post-great-calamity recovery cycle compressed from &quot;epoch-tier&quot; to &quot;generation-tier&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The essence of institutional substitution is dismantling predatory jurisprudence:</p><ul><li><strong>Abolish &quot;capable possess&quot;</strong>: establish joint contracting, more work more pay; resource allocation no longer by fists</li><li><strong>Abolish &quot;other as material&quot;</strong>: demon tribes from body-refining material promoted to equal evolution subject</li><li><strong>Gain indicator</strong>: Myriad-Ranks talent-rate diffuses from &quot;one at the top&quot; to &quot;a generation&quot;</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Injected Institution</th><th>Manghuang Original State</th><th>Post-Injection Gain</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Joint-contracting allocation</td><td>Resources by fists</td><td>Resources by contribution; Myriad Ranks predictable</td></tr><tr><td>20% activation strategy</td><td>Only one Ji Ning produced</td><td>Batch middle tier; no single-top dependency</td></tr><tr><td>Alaya Network</td><td>Lineage goes with the person</td><td>Dao-comprehension perpetual; passing does not break lineage</td></tr><tr><td>Anchor Council</td><td>Order suppressed by Ji Ning</td><td>Collective governance; absence does not collapse</td></tr><tr><td>Anti-predation enshrined</td><td>Zero-sum stock</td><td>Develop increment; do not consume stock</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: inject full symbiotic institutions into Manghuang&#39;s initial world; evolve in parallel with original model</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: compare &quot;original lone-path model&quot; vs. &quot;symbiotic institutions injected&quot; two timelines</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: civilization overall energy curve, Myriad-Ranks talent-rate, great-calamity recovery cycle, Great-Expert-fall transmission rate</li><li><strong>Review conclusion</strong>: after symbiotic institutions injected, civilization overall energy exceeds original model within 500 great-calamity cycles, and has no single-point collapse risk; Ji Ning in the symbiotic model is not &quot;forced to carry it alone,&quot; but one of many middle tier activated by the &quot;20% activation strategy&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>After injection setting self-consistency: high</strong>. Institutions legislated first; rules recomputable</li><li><strong>After injection retcon-ending risk: extremely low</strong></li><li><strong>After injection protagonist uniqueness dependency: extremely low</strong>. Network-style civilization; Ji Ning absent does not affect operation</li></ul><p>Among institutional-substitution gains, the most easily underrated is predictability. In Manghuang&#39;s world, a cultivator does not know tomorrow which Great-Expert battle will affect him; does not know whether his hard-cultivated realm will be devalued by new setting. After symbiotic institutions injected, how resources are allocated, how breakthrough proceeds, whether rules change, are all predictable. Predictability itself is enormous energy — it lets cultivators dare invest ten years, a hundred years in one thing, not ready to flee at any moment. The biggest dividend institutions give is not resources, but peace of mind.</p><p>Institutional-substitution gains also show in risk resistance. The lone-path model can be zeroed by one great calamity; the symbiotic model disperses risk onto institutions; one great calamity is only local loss. The further civilization goes, the larger the gap in risk resistance — this is precisely institutional substitution&#39;s long-term compound interest.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: one-person-monopolized energy dispersed to a generation; civilization total larger</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: abolish fist allocation; establish joint contracting</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo only changed humankind&#39;s lower-middle tier; this institution changes the entire allocation jurisprudence</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: demon tribes promoted to equal subject; Myriad Ranks 99% have a road</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: institutions legislated first; can infinitely expand</li></ul><p>Among institutional-substitution gains there is also an implicit gain: knowledge compound interest. In Manghuang Dao-comprehension goes with the person; every generation starts from zero; under symbiotic institutions Dao-comprehension enters Alaya; every generation stands on the last generation&#39;s shoulders. This knowledge compound interest, the longer the time the larger the advantage — after a hundred generations, symbiotic civilization&#39;s knowledge total is a hundredfold, a thousandfold of Manghuang&#39;s. Institutional gains are not immediate, but become scarier the further along.</p><p>Institutional-substitution gains, the longer the time the more obvious. The first generation sees no difference; the tenth generation pulls away; the thousandth generation is a generational gap. Institutions are compound-interest assets; the older the more valuable.</p><p>Institutional compound interest is the steadiest of all civilization dividends.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Institutional substitution&#39;s gains are not merely &quot;civilization does not collapse,&quot; but &quot;civilization is stronger than before&quot; — because energy monopolized by one person, distributed to a generation to use, the total is actually larger. What Heng Yuan Zhou wants to prove is never &quot;Ji Ning should not be strong,&quot; but &quot;letting Myriad Ranks get strong together is far more cost-effective than letting one person get strong.&quot;</p><p>In the final analysis, Manghuang Ji · institutional-alternative gains · injecting Anchor Symbiosis into Manghuang&#39;s world described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./416_模块2-莽荒纪-求索域复盘-纪宁缺位后的文明崩溃模拟.html">Entry 416 · Quest-Sediment Domain Review</a> · <a href="./418_模块2-莽荒纪-阿赖耶监管方案-杜绝修仙掠夺的制度设计.html">Entry 418 · Alaya Supervision Plan</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/22-资源分配联产承包机制.html">22-Resource Allocation Joint-Contracting Mechanism</a></li></ul>',31)])])}const m=e(a,[["render",s]]);export{h as __pageData,m as default};
